BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Moab Museum": "https://go.theflybook.com/book/1669/EntityConfig/44405%20"}
X-SOURCE-ID:moab_museum
SUMMARY:Living Rivers Expedition: Cataract Canyon
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260708T000000
DTEND;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260711T000000
UID:7b38ce434342ebbe2f64cc8d2acb19d8@moabmuseum.org
DESCRIPTION:Cataract Canyon through Canyonlands National Park is a journey
  into a spectacular\, remote wilderness. This quality multi-faceted advent
 ure is the ideal balance of serenity\, fascination\, and exhilaration – 
 it will elevate your life. And this year\, we are proud to partner with bo
 th Sheri Griffith Adventures\, who is outfitting and organizing this exclu
 sive Cataract Canyon trip\, and John Weisheit of Living Rivers\, who will 
 be the Naturalist on this four-day float. John Weisheit cofounded Living R
 ivers\, based in Moab\, Utah\, in 2000. In 2002\, John became a member of 
 the Waterkeeper Alliance and serves this international organization as the
  Colorado Riverkeeper. He has been a professional river guide and interpre
 ter of natural and human history since 1980. Since 1990\, John has complet
 ed about 75 science-based expeditions to assess the long-term impacts of w
 ater and energy development on the Colorado River\, with a special emphasi
 s on the Colorado Plateau. Secure your spot on this exclusive and limited-
 capacity trip HERE: https://go.theflybook.com/book/1669/EntityConfig/44405
LOCATION:Cataract Canyon\, 
URL:https://go.theflybook.com/book/1669/EntityConfig/44405%20
X-SOURCE:Moab Museum
END:VEVENT
